      "tr": "`for start, end in sorted(intervals, key=lambda iv: iv[0]):`.",
      "en": "`for start, end in sorted(intervals, key=lambda iv: iv[0]):`."
    },
    {
      "tr": "`merged` boş değilse ve `start <= merged[-1][1]` ise sonu `max` ile uzat; değilse `[start, end]` ekle.",
      "en": "If `merged` is not empty and `start <= merged[-1][1]`, extend the end with `max`; otherwise append `[start, end]`."
    },
    {
      "tr": "Çözümün tamamı:\n\n```python\ndef merge_intervals(intervals):\n    merged = []\n    for start, end in sorted(intervals, key=lambda iv: iv[0]):\n        if merged and start <= merged[-1][1]:\n            merged[-1][1] = max(merged[-1][1], end)\n        else:\n            merged.append([start, end])\n    return merged\n\n\nprint(merge_intervals([[8, 10], [1, 3], [2, 6], [15, 18]]))\nprint(merge_intervals([[1, 4], [4, 5]]))\nprint(merge_intervals([]))\n```",
      "en": "The full solution:\n\n```python\ndef merge_intervals(intervals):\n    merged = []\n    for start, end in sorted(intervals, key=lambda iv: iv[0]):\n        if merged and start <= merged[-1][1]:\n            merged[-1][1] = max(merged[-1][1], end)\n        else:\n            merged.append([start, end])\n    return merged\n\n\nprint(merge_intervals([[8, 10], [1, 3], [2, 6], [15, 18]]))\nprint(merge_intervals([[1, 4], [4, 5]]))\nprint(merge_intervals([]))\n```"
    }
